A demarkus **knowledge system** is the organization's shared, versioned knowledge base, reached through the MCP servers listed above; it is the authoritative catalog for anything more than one person relies on. Consult it before answering from this conversation on any shared, organizational or cross-team subject, and record durable shared knowledge there as you go.

## Consult first

Use the joined system's own tools ({{.ToolForm}}); the server's instructions carry the read contract. `/knowledge` lists joined systems and hubs and carries the fallback for an older broker without `mark_lookup_all`. Never fabricate organizational {{.Store}}.

## Record

Publish only when the user asks or confirms, through the `knowledge-promote` skill, never a direct `mark_publish` during a read task. Write-time gates (tags, required axes, retention, style) say what to fix; follow them.

## {{.StoreTitle}} and knowledge system

Personal drafts and machine-local notes live in the {{.Store}}; shared, authoritative knowledge lives in the knowledge system. Draft locally, promote when ready for others; never copy organizational knowledge into the {{.Store}}, link or fetch fresh.